   "frases": [
    {
     "es": "Pero alguien lo había previsto: Prometeo, que todo lo sabía de antemano.",
     "en": "But someone had foreseen it: Prometheus, who knew all things in advance."
    },
    {
     "es": "Avisó a su hijo Deucalión y le dijo que construyera un gran arcón de madera.",
     "en": "He warned his son Deucalion and told him to build a great wooden chest."
    },
    {
     "es": "Deucalión subió con su esposa Pirra, hija de Epimeteo y de Pandora; los dos eran justos.",
     "en": "Deucalion boarded with his wife Pyrrha, daughter of Epimetheus and Pandora; both were righteous."
    },
    {
     "es": "Nueve días y nueve noches flotaron sobre el océano que cubría el mundo, sin ver una sola orilla.",
     "en": "Nine days and nine nights they drifted on the ocean that covered the world, with no shore in sight."
    },
    {
     "es": "Al décimo día, el arcón tocó tierra: la cima del monte Parnaso, lo único que asomaba.",
     "en": "On the tenth day the chest touched ground: the peak of Mount Parnassus, the only land showing."
    }
