   "frases": [
    {
     "es": "Zeus miró el mundo y vio que solo quedaban dos personas, las dos inocentes.",
     "en": "Zeus looked upon the world and saw only two people left, both innocent."
    },
    {
     "es": "Entonces apartó las nubes y mostró de nuevo el cielo a la tierra.",
     "en": "Then he parted the clouds and showed the sky to the earth once more."
    },
    {
     "es": "Poseidón dejó su tridente, y Tritón sopló su caracola para que las aguas se retiraran.",
     "en": "Poseidon lowered his trident, and Triton blew his conch so the waters would retreat."
    },
    {
     "es": "Los ríos volvieron a sus cauces, y las colinas y los árboles reaparecieron cubiertos de barro.",
     "en": "The rivers returned to their beds, and hills and trees reappeared, covered in mud."
    },
    {
     "es": "Pero el mundo estaba vacío y en silencio, y Deucalión y Pirra lloraron de soledad.",
     "en": "But the world was empty and silent, and Deucalion and Pyrrha wept with loneliness."
    }
   ],
