   },
   "frases": [
    {
     "es": "Bajaron del templo y lanzaron piedras por encima del hombro, sin mirar atrás.",
     "en": "They came down from the temple and threw stones over their shoulders, without looking back."
    },
    {
     "es": "Las piedras se ablandaron y tomaron forma, como estatuas que empiezan a esculpirse.",
     "en": "The stones softened and took shape, like statues beginning to be carved."
    },
    {
     "es": "Las que lanzó Deucalión se convirtieron en hombres; las de Pirra, en mujeres.",
     "en": "Those Deucalion threw became men; those Pyrrha threw became women."
    },
    {
     "es": "Por eso los humanos somos una raza dura, capaz de soportar el trabajo y el dolor.",
     "en": "That is why humans are a hardy race, able to endure toil and pain."
    },
    {
     "es": "Deucalión y Pirra tuvieron un hijo, Helén, y de su nombre los griegos se llamaron helenos.",
     "en": "Deucalion and Pyrrha had a son, Hellen, and from his name the Greeks came to be called Hellenes."
    }
